's case 3 above, though is rare in the wild. And of course I might be missing something."],["1cf1009e_2d032f20",18,-1,0,"Agree."],["467972dc_37daf14b",18,-1,1,"Do we get to this situation only when we are calculating the intrinsic size of the flexbox or if a column flexbox has indefinite height?"],["7afbeade_90a397cc",18,-1,0,"Case 1: ``` <div style=\"display: flex; width: 0px;\"> <div style=\"flex: 1 0 0px; width: 200px;\"> <div style=\"width: 100px;\"></div> </div> </div> ``` We DO need content size suggestion but the item's…"]],0,1881],[7247913,20432,19,0.518,0.377,[[1,1562]],[],0,1882],[7248669,20433,28,0.518,0.377,[[1,1563]],[],0,1883],[7249450,20433,17,0.518,0.377,[[1,1564]],[["3a9af8cb_ac552b63",19,0,1,"This will be true if there is 0 or 1 child. The old check would only be true with 1 child. Maybe move the comment above into this block?"]],0,1884],[7251903,20433,5,0.225,0.147,[[1,1565]],[],0,1885],[7254425,20434,20,0.518,0.377,[[1,1566]],[],0,1886],[7251842,20434,74,1.637,1.223,[[1,1567]],[["1d67e6bf_1f8448fb",19,0,1,"Can do this a bit earlier, e.g. before entering the block. But no big deal."]],0,1887],[7253644,20437,15,0.354,0.243,[[1,1568]],[],0,1888],[7262139,20437,162,2.983,2.275,[[1,1569]],[],0,1889],[7244131,20438,129,2.983,2.275,[[1,0.867,1570,113],[0,0.133,575,16]],[["29ade33a_7a3efa80",20,-4,1,"Not sure about `object` vs `sibling`? Why not `previous` / `next`, or `object1` / `object2`? Or should this be a non-static function `void AttemptMergeWithNextSibling()`?…"],["612ed2c6_75bc33d6",20,-4,1,"Should this be a reference instead? None of the overrides check for nullptr."],["cf2627fb_a3aef91d",21,0,0,"This will trigger another call to `AttemptToMerge()` (of `next`'s siblings). Is that a concern? That merge attempt should really not lead to anything, unless the tree is already in a bad state,…"]],0,1890],[7269372,20439,53,0.974,0.711,[[1,1571]],[],0,1891],[7268420,20440,20,0.518,0.377,[[1,1572]],[["803b5037_af42897c",22,0,1,"It's explained in the commit comment, but I think it's worth explaining here as well."]],0,1892],[7268521,20440,15,0.354,0.243,[[1,1573]],[],0,1893],[7277165,20440,10,0.354,0.243,[[1,1574]],[],0,1894],[7271268,20441,155,2.983,2.275,[[1,0.904,1575,142],[0,0.096,576,13]],[["242101de_d2a04b13",8,-1,1,"Also floats. So \"out-of-flow-state\" would be more correct, although \"out-of-flow\" is often taken as either abspos and fixedpos. How about \"in-flow state\" then? Maybe also reflect this in the runtime…"],["b5633b83_b020ac44",13,-1,0,"This can be more expensive than the current implementation in the presence of display:none and display:contents subtrees (assuming the current code only has to work on the box tree?). The…"],["db2695d0_deae27f2",8,-1,1,"or float:left to float:none"],["eb992c8e_cb45f72b",23,-1,1,"If you happen to know why this (and the below) is necessary, please add a comment. I see that this CL disables the corresponding code in StyleDidChange()... But I wish we knew what this is about, and…"],["b62d57c2_e8b3339f",8,3,0,"When relanding, please change this to LayoutReinsertOnInFlowStateChange , which is the new name of the flag."]],0,1895],[7280053,20442,398,4.911,3.884,[[1,1.0,1576,400]],[],0,1896]]}